THIRD-PARTY SOFTWARE

The `rai` binary is statically linked. Every third-party crate it is built from
is compiled into the executables in the release archives, and their license
terms apply to those bytes.

THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md, in this archive and in the repository, reproduces the
full license text of every one of them and names the crates each text covers.
It is generated from the dependency graph of the crate the archives are built
from, and CI fails if the committed copy has drifted from that graph.

Cargo.lock records the exact version of each dependency.
